Sval: Gecko's tooling takes the executable's name from MOZ_APP_NAME

Sval's executable is sval (MOZ_APP_NAME), so that its process name and the
Windows registrations keyed by the executable are not an installed
Firefox's. Mozilla's tooling assumed the name is "firefox" in three places:

- The artifact code looked for firefox/ in every package it unpacks. A
  package's top directory and its binaries are MOZ_APP_NAME
  (package-name.mk, browser/app/moz.build), so it reads that from the
  build. The taskcluster index keeps its own product.
- mozinfo's appname is what the test harnesses and manifests key a
  browser build on: xpcshell's firefox-appdir, mozrunner's FirefoxRunner
  and FirefoxProfile, and appname conditions. A browser build is "firefox"
  to them whatever its executable is called.
- The mochitest harness on Windows treated a live process as the browser
  only when its image was firefox.exe, so it could not find a sval.exe
  left running after a test.

diff --git a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py
index 5bb72e9392..c543ed5215 100644
--- a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py
+++ b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py
@@ -533,6 +533,11 @@ class ArtifactJob:
 
     @property
     def product(self):
+        # A package's top directory and its binaries take the executable's
+        # name (package-name.mk, browser/app/moz.build), which a build can set
+        # apart from the product in the index namespace.
+        if self._substs and "MOZ_APP_NAME" in self._substs:
+            return self._substs["MOZ_APP_NAME"]
         return self.job_configuration.product
 
     @property
diff --git a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py
index 08e9ca8068..0e5817e977 100644
--- a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py
+++ b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py
@@ -44,8 +44,12 @@ def build_dict(config, env=os.environ):
     # Widget toolkit, just pass the value directly through.
     d["toolkit"] = substs.get("MOZ_WIDGET_TOOLKIT")
 
-    # Application name
-    if "MOZ_APP_NAME" in substs:
+    # Application name. The harnesses and manifests know a browser build as
+    # "firefox" (xpcshell's firefox-appdir, mozrunner's FirefoxRunner,
+    # appname conditions), whatever executable name MOZ_APP_NAME gives it.
+    if substs.get("MOZ_BUILD_APP") == "browser":
+        d["appname"] = "firefox"
+    elif "MOZ_APP_NAME" in substs:
         d["appname"] = substs["MOZ_APP_NAME"]
 
     # Build app name
diff --git a/testing/mochitest/runtests.py b/testing/mochitest/runtests.py
index e18b27abf1..5d0070e5c6 100644
--- a/testing/mochitest/runtests.py
+++ b/testing/mochitest/runtests.py
@@ -511,7 +511,9 @@ if mozinfo.isWin:
                 # Still an active process, so conservatively assume it's Firefox.
                 return True
 
-            return pName.value.endswith((b"firefox.exe", b"plugin-container.exe"))
+            return pName.value.endswith(
+                (b"firefox.exe", b"sval.exe", b"plugin-container.exe")
+            )
         finally:
             ctypes.windll.kernel32.CloseHandle(pHandle)
 
